    <p>Security teams are drowning in alert volume. A single SIEM can generate thousands of alerts a day, and most of them follow a predictable pattern: extract an indicator, check it against known threat data, take an action, close the ticket. A Security Orchestration, Automation, and Response platform exists to handle that repetitive work automatically, so analysts spend their time on the judgment calls that actually need a human.</p>

