// TASK 2: What is SOAR?
$task_contents[2] = <<<'HTML'
<div class="content-block">
    <h2>Orchestration, Automation, and Response</h2>

    <p>SOAR stands for <strong>Security Orchestration, Automation, and Response</strong>. It is a platform that connects a SOC's existing tools and runs a defined sequence of steps, called a playbook, whenever a qualifying event occurs.</p>

    <p>Each of the three words in the name describes a distinct job. Orchestration connects tools that would otherwise operate separately. Automation carries out steps without a person clicking through each one. Response is the resulting action taken against the threat, such as isolating a host or blocking an address.</p>

    <div class="info-box">
        <h4><i class="fas fa-info-circle"></i> What SOAR Does Not Replace</h4>
        <p>SOAR removes repetitive manual work, not analyst judgment. Ambiguous cases, novel attack patterns, and decisions with major business impact still need a human in the loop.</p>
    </div>

