    <h2>Feeding and Tracking the Playbook</h2>

    <p>A playbook rarely works with only the data inside the original alert. It needs to pull in context from other systems while it runs, and it needs to leave a record of what happened. Three integrations handle most of that work.</p>

    <p>The SIEM supplies the alert that starts the process. The threat intelligence feed enriches that alert with outside context. The ticketing system tracks the case from open to close.</p>

    <h3>The Three Integrations</h3>
    <table class="content-table">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Integration</th>
                <th>What It Provides</th>
                <th>Example Action</th>
